{
  "slug": "c4m",
  "name": "C4m",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Interactive C4 architecture diagrams (Simon Brown's model) for Claude Code. Five mode-driven\nworkflows — Design (greenfield), Document-code (retro-doc from a repo), Document-prose (from\nREADME/ADR/spec), Review (critique an existing diagram), Update (evolve one) — accessed via\n/c4m:auto, /c4m:design, /c4m:code, /c4m:prose, /c4m:review, /c4m:update. Output is one Markdown\ndocument per C4 level with embedded Mermaid; format negotiable (Structurizr DSL, PlantUML) and\ndestination negotiable (filesystem or MCP — Notion, Linear, Drive). Enforces the editorial\ninvariants: technology mandatory on every Container/Component, intent-specific relationship labels,\nprotocol on inter-container links, assumptions kept explicit.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill** and **6 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `c4-model` (Interactively co-build a software architecture using Simon Brown's C4 model (Context, Container, Component, Code))\n- **Commands** (6): `auto` (Co-build a C4 architecture diagram (Simon Brown's model) interactively), `code` (Retro-document an existing codebase as a C4 diagram), `design` (Design a new system architecture (C4) from scratch via structured dialogue), `prose` (Extract a C4 architecture from prose (README, ADR, spec, meeting transcript)), `review` (Review or explain an existing C4 diagram), `update` (Update an existing C4 diagram — add a container, change a flow, apply review corrections, evolve the architecture)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install c4m@claude-community` from `cheriftj/c4-model-skill`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "command": 6
  },
